<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abraham Kuyper</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1837">1837</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abraham Kuyper was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> Reformed theologian, journalist and politician. He founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anti-revolutionary-party">Anti-Revolutionary Party</a> in 1879, the first modern Dutch political party, and the Free University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amsterdam">Amsterdam</a> in 1880, and served as prime minister from 1901 to 1905. His idea of 'sphere <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sovereignty">sovereignty</a>' helped shape the pillarisation of Dutch society into separate Protestant, Catholic and secular communities.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abraham-kuyper.jpg" alt="Abraham Kuyper" width="320" height="457" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Abraham_Kuyper_1905_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
